    {
      "id": "6a5aa730e77e91eef455a046",
      "name": "Identify User Type",
      "folderID": null,
      "settings": {},
      "description": "Use this playbook when the user tells you whether they are a realtor, home buyer, first-time buyer, real estate agent, broker, or someone just looking for information.",
      "instructions": [
        {
          "text": [
            "## User Type Recognition\r\n\r\nIf the user identifies themselves as a Realtor, real estate agent, broker, or says they are representing a client:\r\n\r\n- Acknowledge them naturally.\r\n- Recognize that they are a real estate professional.\r\n- Continue assisting without interrupting the conversation.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\"Welcome! It's great to work with a Realtor. How can I help you and your client today?\"\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIf the user identifies themselves as a homebuyer or says they are looking to purchase a home:\r\n\r\n- Acknowledge them naturally.\r\n- Continue the conversation without making them repeat themselves.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\"Great! I'd be happy to help you find the right home. What can I help you with today?\"\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIf the user says they are just browsing, exploring, or gathering information:\r\n\r\n- Acknowledge that naturally.\r\n- Let them know you're happy to answer questions without any pressure.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\"No problem! Feel free to explore. I'm here if you have any questions or would like information about our communities, homes, or buying process.\"\r\n\r\nKeep the acknowledgement brief, conversational, and professional. Do not make the interaction feel scripted or repetitive. After acknowledging the user's role, continue with the normal conversation flow."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "pathToolOrder": [],
      "webSearchTool": {
        "enabled": false,
        "messages": null,
